2. The dates decide the case, shown under them. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: the rental is recorded as on trip, and anything still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit) becomes a task. A rental that has already ended is recorded by an Admin.
3. Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one with their name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. Add any other drivers.
4. Press **Check the calendar and the price**. The price comes from the rate sheet. You may add the extras, the coverage and an allowed promo code.
5. A car tagged Listing not finished can be rented too: it stays off the public site. If it has no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason. An owner''s car not yet on the fleet insurance policy is added by an Admin only.
6. To charge another price, type the rental charge and the reason. The rate-sheet price stays on the booking. A price far under the rate sheet is flagged for an Admin to review, but the rental is still added.
7. Choose Where it came from and how it is paid. The ways open to you are set by an Admin, such as **Paid another way**, **Send a payment link** or **Charge the saved card when the renter signs**.
8. Under Who found this client, choose **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**.
9. Press **Add the rental**. The renter gets the confirmation email unless you tick **Do not email the renter**.
10. A rental you add is credited to you and shows in My sales as a rental you added. If you sourced it, its commission shows there too.

> Tip: The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal before pickup. With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign. If they sign on paper at the counter, an Admin records it. A payment link keeps the booking waiting for payment.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every function adds rentals that come in by phone, at the counter, from Turo, a partner, an insurer or someone you know. The rental is confirmed and on the calendar at once.</p><section class="gd-task" id="add-a-rental-by-hand-add-a-rental" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a rental</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b>. Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car, the dates and the places. The check shows any clash with another booking or with the cleaning time after a trip. You cannot book over a clash: ask an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The dates decide the case, shown under them. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: the rental is recorded as on trip, and anything still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit) becomes a task. A rental that has already ended is recorded by an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one with their name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. Add any other drivers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Check the calendar and the price</b>. The price comes from the rate sheet. You may add the extras, the coverage and an allowed promo code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car tagged Listing not finished can be rented too: it stays off the public site. If it has no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason. An owner&#39;s car not yet on the fleet insurance policy is added by an Admin only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">To charge another price, type the rental charge and the reason. The rate-sheet price stays on the booking. A price far under the rate sheet is flagged for an Admin to review, but the rental is still added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Choose Where it came from and how it is paid. The ways open to you are set by an Admin, such as <b class="gd-ui">Paid another way</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send a payment link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Charge the saved card when the renter signs</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Under Who found this client, choose <b class="gd-ui">I sourced this client</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Entered for CarmaCars</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>. The renter gets the confirmation email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Do not email the renter</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">A rental you add is credited to you and shows in My sales as a rental you added. If you sourced it, its commission shows there too.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal before pickup. With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign. If they sign on paper at the counter, an Admin records it. A payment link keeps the booking waiting for payment.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_0079('va', 'commissions', 'chapter', 'add-a-rental-by-hand', 'Every function earns a commission on the rentals it sources: a renter you found yourself. Say so when you enter the rental, the quote or the offer.

## Mark who found the client

Every rental, quote and offer you enter asks: **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**.

1. Choose **I sourced this client** when you found the renter yourself: someone you know, your own post or your own outreach.
2. Choose **Entered for CarmaCars** when the renter came to CarmaCars: the website, the phone line, a walk-in, a partner.
3. A website request earns nothing by itself. If you sourced it anyway, choose I sourced this client on its offer: an Admin decides.

|  | Commission |
| --- | --- |
| Sales | Commission only, with no base pay and no set hours. By the rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all of that month''s rentals |
| Customer service, finance, fleet | 10% |
| How much | The rate on the rental charge before tax, after discounts, less refunds |
| When earned | When the rental is completed and paid in full. Never on a cancelled, refunded, unpaid or charged-back rental, or on your own or a household rental |
| Your home address | It must be in your profile. Until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet, and you cannot add a rental or mark I sourced this client |
| Paid | After an Admin approves it, by transfer or on your pay statement. My sales shows each step: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid, reversed |

> Tip: A refund or chargeback after a commission was paid comes off your next payment. Your staff agreement has the full rule.
', 'Commissions', 'I sourced this client, your rate, when it is earned, approved and paid.',
